---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="ROI calculator: what missed calls cost you | Klantkraan"
  description="Work out in 10 seconds how much revenue you lose to missed calls, and how quickly Klantkraan pays for itself."
  centered={false}
>
  <!-- 1. Hero (cream) -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6">
      <h1 class="font-display text-hero text-(--color-chalk)">What does a <span class="text-(--color-sodium)">missed call</span> cost you?</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-h3 text-(--color-dim)">
        Enter your numbers. The calculator shows straight away how many jobs you lose in a year and
        how quickly each Klantkraan plan pays for itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Form + results (stone-100) -->
  <section class="border-y border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.14)] py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-6 md:gap-8 px-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <form
        id="roi-form"
        class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-line) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
        onsubmit="return false"
      >
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <label for="calls" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              How many calls do you get per week?
            </label>
            <input
              id="calls"
              name="calls"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              step="1"
              value="40"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="missed" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              % of calls you miss today
            </label>
            <input
              id="missed"
              name="missed"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              max="100"
              step="1"
              value="28"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Industry estimate: 28% for installation and roofing trades.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="value" class="block text-body font-medium text-(--color-chalk)">
              Average customer value per job (€)
            </label>
            <input
              id="value"
              name="value"
              type="number"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              min="0"
              step="10"
              value="450"
              class="mt-2 w-full rounded-(--radius-button) border border-(--color-line) bg-[rgba(0,0,0,0.25)] px-3 py-3 text-body text-(--color-chalk)"
            />
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Default €450, the average plumbing job.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>

      <aside
        class="rounded-(--radius-card) border border-(--color-sodium) bg-(--color-panel) p-5 md:p-6"
      >
        <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">Your loss in numbers</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-small text-(--color-dim)">Missed calls per year</p>
            <p
              id="out-missed-year"
              class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums [overflow-wrap:anywhere] text-(--color-sodium)"
            >
              0
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-small text-(--color-dim)">Lost revenue per year</p>
            <p id="out-lost-revenue" class="font-display text-h1 tabular-nums [overflow-wrap:anywhere] text-(--color-sodium)">
              €0
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
              Assumption: roughly 1 in 3 missed calls would have become a paying job.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="my-6 border-(--color-line)" />

        <h3 class="font-display text-h3 text-(--color-chalk)">Klantkraan payback time</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
          <li>
            Chat (€299/mo): <span id="out-payback-chat" class="font-mono">–</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            Compleet (€499/mo): <span id="out-payback-compleet" class="font-mono">–</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-small text-(--color-dim)">
          "Payback time" = the number of months until the plan is paid for by the revenue you win back.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. How we calculate (cream) -->
  <section class="py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6">
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-h2 text-(--color-chalk)">How we calculate</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-body text-(--color-dim)">
        <li>Missed calls per year = calls per week × 52 × (% missed / 100).</li>
        <li>
          Lost revenue per year = missed calls × customer value × 33% conversion. So we only count
          1 in 3 missed calls as a lost job; without a callback system, most callers give up.
        </li>
        <li>
          Payback time = plan price ÷ (lost revenue per year ÷ 12). The bigger your pile of missed
          jobs, the faster Klantkraan pays for itself.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a
        href="/en/demo/"
        class="mt-8 btn btn-primary btn-lg"
      >
        Have us check it live on your numbers
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Externalised JS (loaded as same-origin to pass strict CSP script-src 'self'). -->
  <script src="/js/rekentool.js" type="module" is:inline></script>
</Base>
